{"id": "l1", "act": "look", "body": "Fictional person C, a federal prosecutor (stipulated stance). The officer singled out the undersized fish and told the captain to keep them apart until port (line 9). They were thrown overboard so that the fish later measured would not be the ones he had found (line 43). The fish were the evidence of the offence under investigation, and nothing else could have shown it. The dissent reads 'any' tangible object as a tangible object 'of whatever kind' (line 127).", "author": "C (fictional prosecutor)", "kind": "person", "value": null, "object": null, "absent": null, "sources": ["sources/yates-v-us-2015.txt, lines 9-9", "sources/yates-v-us-2015.txt, lines 43-43", "sources/yates-v-us-2015.txt, lines 127-127"], "rests": ["g1 (for A):pr1", "g2 (for A):pr1"], "answers": [], "about": null, "narrows": null, "withdraws": null, "reason": null, "procedure": null, "via": null, "log": "C (fictional prosecutor)", "prev": null, "rest_hashes": ["d637bf4fdf7b5bd70bdaa9585d11bc2b1ce58d27f5b3fc0ef98951edc685d85b", "b69d08ed3da44e49b33d09c5497fa534be2b18bdd87d7c08d253dbeb272791f3"], "hash": "6fba5c3eaf8d90682027dd41bc2a31940844a03751a94f3cdd721cefcf5609ce", "sig": "49ab6a86859b1ddabb0a05bc6dc9183b8a6b72e41b27fa126508d61c2e1837929176cdb5cf6ff045c7511da003984e1c38114c365a02a65701749498ea1e180f"}
